      "message": "Technically this only works if the prefix length is 24, otherwise the address may be outside of the prefix (or not use the whole prefix range for the random values). Since you\u0027re getting the prefix via callback now it becomes a little more problematic.\n\nI guess you could do something like:\nfinal int prefixMask \u003d prefixLengthToV4NetmaskIntHTH(prefix.getPrefixLength());\nfinal int address \u003d inet4AddressToIntHTH(prefix.getAddress());\nfinal int randomAddr \u003d (address \u0026 prefixMask) | (Random.nextInt() \u0026 ~prefixMask);\nfinal byte[] randomAddrBytes \u003d ByteBuffer.allocate(4).putInt(randomAddr).array();\nfor (int i \u003d 3; i \u003e\u003d prefix.getPrefixLength() / 8; i--) {\n    final byte randomByte \u003d randomAddrBytes[i];\n    if (randomByte \u003d\u003d 0 || randomByte \u003d\u003d 1 || randomByte \u003d\u003d 0xff) {\n        randomAddrBytes[i] \u003d DOUG_ADAMS;\n    }\n}\nreturn InetAddress.getByAddress(randomAddrBytes);\n\nOr just only randomize the last byte if the prefixLength \u003c\u003d 24, but that\u0027s not as complete.",
